@startuml post_update_flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Inter, Segoe UI, sans-serif"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam shadowout false

skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 150

skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    BorderColor #64748B
    FontColor #0F172A
    FontSize 11
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontSize 10
}

skinparam activityDiamond {
    BackgroundColor #FEF3C7
    BorderColor #D97706
    FontColor #92400E
}

title **Modern Laravel Blog - Author Dashboard: Post Update & Policy Authorization Flow**

|#EFF6FF|Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
|#F0FDF4|PostPolicy Authorization|
|#FEFCE8|DashboardPostController|
|#FAF5FF|Storage (Public Disk) & SQLite DB|

|Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
start
:Author clicks "Edit" button on a post row in Dashboard;
:Navigate to **GET /dashboard/posts/{post}/edit**;

|PostPolicy Authorization|
:Execute **Gate::authorize('update', $post)**;
:Evaluate **PostPolicy@update(User $user, Post $post)**:
""return $user->id === $post->author_id"";

if (Is Authenticated User the Post Author?) then (no - Unauthorized)
    |PostPolicy Authorization|
    :Abort with **403 Forbidden Error**\n("This action is unauthorized."); <<#FEE2E2>>
    stop
else (yes - Authorized)
    |DashboardPostController|
    :Fetch categories list:\n""Category::orderBy('name')->get()"";
    :Pass **$post** and **$categories** to view **dashboard.posts.edit**;

    |Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
    :Initialize Alpine.js scope prefilled with existing model attributes:
    - Title, Slug, Category, Body
    - Current image thumbnail (if present on storage);
    :Author modifies fields or uploads a replacement image;
    :Author clicks "Update Article" button;
    :Submit form via **PUT /dashboard/posts/{post}**\nwith **@method('PUT')** and **@csrf**;

    |PostPolicy Authorization|
    :Re-verify **Gate::authorize('update', $post)**;
    if (Authorized?) then (no)
        :Abort with 403 Forbidden; <<#FEE2E2>>
        stop
    else (yes)
        |DashboardPostController|
        :Execute Validation with exception for current post ID:
        - **title**: required | string | max:255
        - **slug**: required | string | max:255 | alpha_dash | unique:posts,slug,{post->id}
        - **category_id**: required | exists:categories,id
        - **body**: required | string
        - **image**: nullable | image | mimes:jpeg,png,jpg,webp,gif | max:2048;

        if (Validation Passed?) then (no)
            |Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
            :Redirect back to edit form with validation error bag; <<#FEE2E2>>
            stop
        else (yes)
            |DashboardPostController|
            if (Author selected a new image file?) then (yes)
                |Storage (Public Disk) & SQLite DB|
                if (Old image exists on disk?) then (yes)
                    :Delete old image from storage:\n""Storage::disk('public')->delete($post->image)"";
                else (no)
                    :No previous image to delete;
                endif
                :Store replacement image on public disk:\n""$validated['image'] = $request->file('image')->store('posts', 'public')"";
            else (no)
                |DashboardPostController|
                :Keep existing image path;
            endif

            |Storage (Public Disk) & SQLite DB|
            :Execute database update:\n""$post->update($validated)"";
            :Update **posts** table record and timestamps in SQLite;

            |DashboardPostController|
            :Flash message: **with('success', 'Article updated successfully!')**;
            :Redirect to **route('dashboard.posts.index')**;

            |Author (Browser & Alpine.js)|
            :Display Dashboard table with updated article details\nand auto-dismissing success alert; <<#DCFCE7>>
            stop
        endif
    endif
endif

@enduml
